  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "Use dry play sand only; damp sand goes mouldy and splits the bags. If a bag is clumped, spread it on a tarp in the sun first. Wear the dust mask whenever you pour.",
    "Put one poly sandbag inside another to make a double-wall bag, stand it in a bucket on the bathroom scale, and scoop in sand to 10 lb.",
    "Squeeze the air out, twist the two necks together, close them with two cable ties, fold the tail down and wrap the whole bag tightly in duct tape.",
    "Repeat until you have eight 10 lb fill bags (80 lb in total).",
    "Load two to eight fill bags into the duffel for 20 to 80 lb, packed tight so they do not shift, and close it.",
    "Check the tape and ties each month and replace any fill bag at the first sign of a leak."
  ],
